{
 "manufacturer": "Ecoforest",
 "manufacturer_slug": "ecoforest",
 "model": "ecoGEO / ecoAIR heat pump (API HP24 Client, Modbus RTU)",
 "model_slug": "ecogeo-ecoair-hp24",
 "short_model": "ecoGEO / ecoAIR HP24",
 "aliases": [
  "ecoGEO",
  "ecoGEO B&C",
  "ecoGEO HP",
  "ecoAIR",
  "AWD24",
  "WWD24",
  "WWC24",
  "API HP24_V01.02"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Heat pump",
 "applies_to": "Ecoforest ecoGEO, ecoGEO HP and ecoAIR heat pumps on software AWD24, WWD24, WWC24 or later, register list API HP24_V01.02 (heat pump list only; supervisor and source-manager lists not included).",
 "summary": "Ecoforest's geothermal and air-source heat pumps expose the 'API HP Client' list over Modbus RTU on the BMS2 RS-485 port. Every value is a single 16-bit holding register with a fixed gain. This map covers status, alarms, compressor counters, humidity, service powers and the read/write BUS control and setpoint registers; temperature and pressure readings are left out because the manual does not state their sign.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 17,
  "baud": 19200,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": 2,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "0-based",
  "note": "Addresses are printed in decimal and go on the wire unchanged: the manual's read example for outdoor temperature (address 2080) sends start register 08 20 hex, and the write example for heat pump status (2700) sends 0A 8C hex."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": "Heat pump software AWD24 / WWD24 / WWC24 and later; API HP24_V01.02",
 "source": {
  "title": "APIs BUS Client Manual (API HP Client manual)",
  "doc_number": "V03",
  "revision_date": "2024-12",
  "url": "https://taphome.com/compatibility/devices/ecoforest-hp24/manufacturer/manual-api-bus-client.pdf",
  "unofficial": true,
  "pages": "pp. 7-10 (port, enable, Modbus functions, frame examples); pp. 14-27 (heat pump register list, section 4)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Ecoforest does not appear to host this manual publicly; the link is an unaltered copy of the Ecoforest manual on the TapHome integration site.",
  "The manual calls every BUS register a 16-bit analog value but never states whether it is signed, and prints no range for the temperature, pressure, DT, superheat and final-setpoint readings. Those readings (2080-2102, 2130-2144, 2150-2164) are therefore left out, as are the cooling setpoints 2723 and 2731-2739 whose lower limit is only given as T_lim. Writable setpoints whose printed range is entirely positive are listed as UINT16 (identical decoding inside that range); only 2777/2778, printed as -99.9 to 99.9 kW, are INT16. Humidity 2170-2174 is listed as UINT16 because relative humidity cannot be negative.",
  "Instantaneous powers 2186-2194 are left unscaled because their gain depends on register 2185 (W = 1, kW or MW = 0.1).",
  "Left out: the energy-meter block 2200-2461 (gain depends on per-period unit registers) and e-MANAGER power readings 2501-2508, model-code digit registers 2010-2023 and software version letters 2007-2009, and the duplicate 'Zone n temperature' entries at 2175-2179 whose meaning differs from 2140-2144 but is not explained.",
  "The heat pump status read (2045: 0 off, 1 on, 2 emergency) and the command register (2700: 1 off, 2 on, 3 emergency) use different codes; operation program likewise (2044 0-2, 2701 1-3).",
  "Software older than AWD24 / WWD24 / WWC24 is not compatible with this register list."
 ],
